# Mobile release versioning

When the user asks to build an APK, ship a release, or bump the app version:

1. Edit `mobile/appVersion.js` only (single source of truth):
   - Bump `version` (SemVer, e.g. `1.0.1` → `1.0.2` for fixes, `1.1.0` for features)
   - Always increment `versionCode` by 1 (Android integer; never reuse)
2. Sync `mobile/package.json` `"version"` to the same SemVer string
3. Keep `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` in `mobile/eas.json` aligned with the live server (must end with `/api`)
4. APK artifact name is produced as `Hollow Ver-{version}.apk` via `plugins/withHollowAndroid.js`

Do not leave `version` / `versionCode` unchanged across a new store or sideload build the user asked for.
